\pard\sb0\sa240\qc\b\f0\fs32\cf1 MARKER SPACE CHECK\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\keepn\b\f0\fs22\cf2 PURPOSE\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\b0\f0\fs20\cf0 Scans selected books for character-style markers (read from usfm.sty and the project's custom.sty), plus {\f1\\f} (footnote) and {\f1\\x} (cross-reference), and flags spacing problems around each opening/closing marker pair. Each occurrence is reported both as a results-list entry (with reference and text snippet, like other checks) and as a line in a detailed HTML report ({\f1 MarkerSpaceReport.html}), written to the project folder and opened automatically when the check finishes.\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\f0\fs20 Marker codes starting with {\f1\\t} are ignored by default (table/structure markers such as {\f1\\tc1} or {\f1\\tr}), except {\f1\\tl} (a genuine character-style pair) and {\f1\\ts-s}/{\f1\\ts-e} (USFM 3 section milestones), which are never silently excluded even though they aren't independently spacing-checked by this tool.\par
\pard\sb240\sa80\keepn\b\f0\fs22\cf2 CHECKS PERFORMED\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\b0\f0\fs20 1.\tab{\b Missing space before opening marker}\emdash e.g. {\f1 word\\nd} instead of {\f1 word \\nd}.\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\f0\fs20 2.\tab{\b Unwanted space before opening marker}\emdash for markers listed in NoSpaceBeforeMarkers (default {\f1\\f}, {\f1\\x}), which conventionally attach directly to the preceding word with no space.\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\f0\fs20 3.\tab{\b Unwanted space before closing marker}\emdash e.g. {\f1\\nd word \\nd*} instead of {\f1\\nd word\\nd*}.\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\f0\fs20 4.\tab{\b Missing space after closing marker}\emdash the closing marker is glued directly to the following word with no space.\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\f0\fs20 5.\tab{\b Unwanted space before punctuation after closing marker}\emdash e.g. {\f1\\nd* ,} instead of {\f1\\nd*,}. This rule is the same regardless of any other option.\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\f0\fs20 6.\tab{\b Unclosed marker}\emdash an opening marker with no matching closing marker found before the end of the chapter.\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\f0\fs20 7.\tab{\b Unexpected closing marker}\emdash a closing marker found for a marker listed in NoCloseMarkers (markers that don't normally take one at all, e.g. {\f1\\v}, {\f1\\xk}, {\f1\\fp}).\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\f0\fs20{\i Note:} punctuation directly after a closing marker is always normal (never flagged), and so is a closing marker immediately followed by another closing marker (nested character styles ending together, e.g. {\f1\\+nd*\\add*}) -- any real problem there belongs to that outer marker's own check.\par
\pard\sb240\sa80\keepn\b\f0\fs22\cf2 HOW TO USE\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\b0\f0\fs20 1.\tab Copy the .cms and .py files to your My Paratext 9 Projects\\cms folder.\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\f0\fs20 2.\tab In Paratext, run the check from Project menu > Tools > Custom Tools > Phil_new.\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\f0\fs20 3.\tab Review the results list for each flagged occurrence, then open the full HTML report (written to the project folder and launched automatically) for summary counts and grouped examples.\par
\pard\sb240\sa80\keepn\b\f0\fs22\cf2 OPTIONS\par
\pard\li360\sb160\sa0\keepn\b\f1\fs20\cf3 ExcludeMarkers\par
\pard\li720\sb60\sa0\b0\f0\fs20{\b Default:}  {\i (empty)}\par
\pard\li720\sb40\sa80\f0\fs20 Marker codes, separated by spaces, to skip entirely (e.g.  w rq ), for markers that follow a different spacing convention in this project.\par
\pard\li360\sb160\sa0\keepn\b\f1\fs20\cf3 NoCloseMarkers\par
\pard\li720\sb60\sa0\b0\f0\fs20{\b Default:}  {\i v fk fp fq fqa ft fr xk xo xq}\par
\pard\li720\sb40\sa80\f0\fs20 Marker codes, separated by spaces, that don't normally take a closing marker in any context. These are skipped by checks 1-5 above; if a closing marker is nonetheless found for one, it's reported separately (check 7).\par
\pard\li360\sb160\sa0\keepn\b\f1\fs20\cf3 NoCloseInNoteMarkers\par
\pard\li720\sb60\sa0\b0\f0\fs20{\b Default:}  {\i xt}\par
\pard\li720\sb40\sa80\f0\fs20 Marker codes, separated by spaces, that only skip requiring a closing marker when nested inside a footnote ({\f1\\f...\\f*}) or cross-reference ({\f1\\x...\\x*}) span. Used on their own elsewhere, they're checked normally like any other marker, including requiring their own closing marker.\par
\pard\li360\sb160\sa0\keepn\b\f1\fs20\cf3 ExtraSpacingMarkers\par
\pard\li720\sb60\sa0\b0\f0\fs20{\b Default:}  {\i f x}\par
\pard\li720\sb40\sa80\f0\fs20 Marker codes, separated by spaces, to check for spacing even though they aren't StyleType Character in usfm.sty. {\f1\\f} and {\f1\\x} are Note-type markers by default but should still follow normal open/close spacing conventions.\par
\pard\li360\sb160\sa0\keepn\b\f1\fs20\cf3 NoSpaceBeforeMarkers\par
\pard\li720\sb60\sa0\b0\f0\fs20{\b Default:}  {\i f x}\par
\pard\li720\sb40\sa0\f0\fs20 Marker codes, separated by spaces, that conventionally attach directly to the preceding word or punctuation with no space (footnote and cross-reference callers). For these, a space before the marker is the anomaly instead of the usual missing-space check.\par
\pard\li720\sb0\sa80\f0\fs20{\f1\\f} is automatically removed from this list when FootnotePrecedesText (below) is set to Yes.\par
\pard\li360\sb160\sa0\keepn\b\f1\fs20\cf3 FootnotePrecedesText\par
\pard\li720\sb60\sa0\b0\f0\fs20{\b Default:}  {\i No}\par
\pard\li720\sb40\sa80\f0\fs20 Set to Yes if this project's convention places the footnote marker BEFORE the word it annotates, rather than after. Reverses the {\f1\\f} spacing checks: a space is expected before {\f1\\f}, and no space is expected after {\f1\\f*} (a stray space directly before punctuation is still always flagged either way -- see check 5). Does not affect {\f1\\x}.\par
\pard\li360\sb160\sa0\keepn\b\f1\fs20\cf3 MaxExamples\par
\pard\li720\sb60\sa0\b0\f0\fs20{\b Default:}  {\i 25}\par
\pard\li720\sb40\sa80\f0\fs20 Caps how many example references are listed under each section of the HTML report. Total counts shown in the report are unaffected.\par
}
